<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Demetrias</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 293 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Demetrias was a Greek city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pagasetic-gulf">Pagasetic Gulf</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a>, near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volos">Volos</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/demetrius-i-of-macedon">Demetrius Poliorcetes</a> around 293 BCE by merging the populations of nearby towns. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalcis">Chalcis</a> and Corinth it was one of the 'fetters of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>', the fortresses through which the Antigonid kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> controlled Greece. Its ruins lie south of Volos.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/demetrias.jpg" alt="Demetrias" width="320" height="289" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thessaly.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
